We investigate the impact of $b 	o c$ decay data on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay within the $U_1$ leptoquark model. The $U_1$ leptoquark model, which is based on the $SU(2)_L$ gauge symmetry, is capable of explaining the $B$ meson anomalies and the lepton universality violation observed in $B$ decays. The model's $U_1$ leptoquark can also account for the $b 	o c$ decay anomalies, but its influence on the $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ decay is minimal. The $U_1$ leptoquark model predicts a branching ratio for $\Lambda_b 	o p 	au  ar{
u}$ that is significantly lower than the Standard Model prediction, which is in conflict with the LHCb measurement.
